1
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:16,930
Hello everybody, welcome back to the IELTS Intermediate Speaking Course by PREP.

2
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:24,630
In today's lesson, I'm going to share with you a very useful

3
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:30,130
technique called FER, which helps expand our ideas and make our answers longer.

4
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:35,170
In this technique, after answering a speaking part one question by giving

5
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:39,970
a general direct answer, we will extend our answer by providing information

6
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:42,470
from one or more of the following categories.

7
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:48,910
F is for feeling, E - example, R for reason.

8
00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:50,830
Let's look at an example. 

9
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:52,770
Do you have any hobbies?

10
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:56,410
First, we provide a direct answer to the question.

11
00:00:57,010 --> 00:01:00,010
I will say that I have a hobby, which is woodworking.

12
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:03,310
Then we can express our F, feeling.

13
00:01:03,879 --> 00:01:07,430
To be specific, we talk about what the hobby makes us feel.

14
00:01:08,230 --> 00:01:11,990
I will say that this hobby makes me feel energized, and then

15
00:01:11,990 --> 00:01:16,770
I further explain that it helps me relieve stress and gives me a great sense of enjoyment.

16
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:21,590
Next, I compare the current feeling with the feeling before I started

17
00:01:21,590 --> 00:01:24,110
this hobby to further extend the answer.

18
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:29,850
It also allows me to use the simple past tense to show the examiner more grammatical structures.

19
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:34,690
Feeling before, depressed due to having too much on my plate.

20
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:36,490
I always felt depressed.

21
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:37,070
Why?

22
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:39,990
Because I had too many things to do.

23
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:46,030
Next, let's apply the FER technique to the second question by providing

24
00:01:46,030 --> 00:01:49,550
a general answer and then extending it using an example.

25
00:01:50,590 --> 00:01:51,930
What are the benefits of hobbies?

26
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:55,450
For this question, I will give a general first.

27
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:57,950
There are many benefits of having a hobby.

28
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:03,310
Then, I'll provide an example of a specific hobby and the benefit it has on me.

29
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:06,590
I'll give you 10 seconds to think of your own example.

30
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:08,690
10 seconds starting now.

31
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:22,100
Finished?

32
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:23,900
Here's my example.

33
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:28,340
I started playing tennis when I graduated from university, and it helped

34
00:02:28,340 --> 00:02:33,560
me relieve stress after work, improve my physical health, and boost my confidence.

35
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:38,400
Here, I provide an example in the past to use the simple past tense.

36
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,680
Do you understand better now?

37
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:45,400
Let's move on to the third question and provide a general and direct answer.

38
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:49,220
Then expand it by adding R, reason.

39
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:52,420
Is it harmful to spend too much time on a hobby?

40
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:55,840
First, I'll answer with a simple yes.

41
00:02:56,580 --> 00:03:00,880
Then I provide a reason why spending too much time on a hobby can be harmful.

42
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,440
I'll give you 10 seconds to think of a reason.

43
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,000
10 seconds starting now.

44
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,560
Have you come up with any reason?

45
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,060
Here's my reason.

46
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:25,520
Spending too much time on a hobby can be harmful because it

47
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,660
may lead to negligence of work and relationships, which constrain important

48
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:32,120
connections and affect my professional life.

49
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:38,300
So, now we've learned an effective technique for expanding our ideas for speaking part one questions.

50
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:46,420
Now, let's listen to my sample answers and read them out loud.

51
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,180
Do you have any hobbies?

52
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:49,580
Yes, I do.

53
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:53,140
Recently, I've tried out a new hobby, woodworking.

54
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:56,980
I have felt incredibly energized as this past time has helped me

55
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:00,140
relieve stress and bring me a great sense of pleasure.

56
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:04,380
In contrast to how I used to feel, often depressed by the

57
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:08,900
to-do lists that were always growing and the constant sense of having too much on my plate.

58
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:13,020
Let's pause the video and read out loud the sample answer.

59
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:20,089
What are the benefits of hobbies?

60
00:04:20,730 --> 00:04:22,930
There are a few perks of partaking in hobbies.

61
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:27,530
I picked up tennis after graduating from university and has become an

62
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:32,090
immensely pleasurable task, which helps me relieve stress after work.

63
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:37,110
Additionally, as a form of workout, it also contributes to improving my

64
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:42,090
physical health, consequently giving me a tremendous confident boost.

65
00:04:42,890 --> 00:04:46,130
Let's pause the video and read out loud the sample answer.

66
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:54,140
Is it harmful to spend too much time on a hobby?

67
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:58,960
Yes, spending an excessive amount of time partaking in a hobby is

68
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:03,360
correlated to the negligence of other life priorities, such as work and

69
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:08,540
relationships, which constrain individuals' important connections and professional life.

70
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:12,660
Let's pause the video and read out loud the sample answer.

71
00:05:22,450 --> 00:05:27,790
Today, we learned the F-E-R technique to expand our answers in IELTS speaking.

72
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:32,970
After giving our answer, we can add feeling, example, and reason.

73
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:35,350
Good job, everyone.

74
00:05:36,190 --> 00:05:39,450
Remember to review this lesson and finish all the exercises.

75
00:05:40,390 --> 00:05:41,310
Until next time, everyone.

